# ARCHITECTURE - Clean Architecture + MVVM + DDD (voy-app-react-native)

> **Versão**: 1.0.0
> **Status**: Ativo

Este documento contém a estrutura de pastas e os templates para implementar novas features seguindo **Clean Architecture**, com **MVVM** na camada de apresentação e princípios de **DDD** no domínio.

## 📐 Princípio Central: Regra de Dependência

```
presentation ──┐
               ├──> domain (nao depende de nada)
data ──────────┘
```

- `domain` é puro TypeScript: **nunca** importa React, React Native, axios/fetch, AsyncStorage, ou qualquer coisa de `data`/`presentation`.
- `data` implementa os contratos (interfaces) definidos em `domain`.
- `presentation` consome `domain` (via UseCases) e nunca acessa `data` diretamente.
- Cada feature é um **bounded context (DDD)**: pode ter suas próprias entidades mesmo que outra feature tenha um conceito parecido — não force compartilhamento prematuro.

## 📁 Folder Structure Template

Para qualquer nova feature, use esta estrutura:

```
src/features/[featureName]/
├── domain/
│   ├── entities/
│   │   └── [Nome]Entity.ts
│   ├── repositories/
│   │   └── [Nome]Repository.ts        # interface (contrato)
│   └── usecases/
│       ├── Get[Nome]UseCase.ts
│       └── [Verbo][Nome]UseCase.ts     # um arquivo por acao de negocio
├── data/
│   ├── datasources/
│   │   └── [Nome]RemoteDataSource.ts
│   ├── models/
│   │   └── [Nome]Dto.ts                # DTO + mapper para/da Entity
│   └── repositories/
│       └── [Nome]RepositoryImpl.ts     # implementa a interface do domain
├── presentation/
│   ├── screens/
│   │   └── [FeatureName]Screen.tsx     # View: fábrica + render puro
│   ├── components/
│   │   └── [ComponentName]/
│   └── viewmodels/
│       └── use[FeatureName].ts         # ViewModel: hook que chama UseCases
└── __tests__/
    ├── domain/
    ├── data/
    └── presentation/
```

Código usado por 2+ features vai para `src/shared/` com as mesmas subpastas (`domain/`, `data/`, `presentation/`, mais `utils/`). Composição/DI e configuração técnica global ficam em `src/core/`.

## 🛠️ File Templates

### 1. Entity (domain/entities)

```typescript
// domain/entities/PlaceEntity.ts
export interface PlaceEntity {
  id: string
  name: string
  description: string
  coordinates: Coordinates
}

export interface Coordinates {
  latitude: number
  longitude: number
}
```

### 2. Repository - Interface (domain/repositories)

```typescript
// domain/repositories/PlaceRepository.ts
import { PlaceEntity } from '../entities/PlaceEntity'

export interface PlaceRepository {
  getList(): Promise<PlaceEntity[]>
  getById(id: string): Promise<PlaceEntity | null>
}
```

### 3. UseCase (domain/usecases)

```typescript
// domain/usecases/GetPlaceListUseCase.ts
import { PlaceEntity } from '../entities/PlaceEntity'
import { PlaceRepository } from '../repositories/PlaceRepository'

export class GetPlaceListUseCase {
  constructor(private readonly placeRepository: PlaceRepository) {}

  async execute(): Promise<PlaceEntity[]> {
    return this.placeRepository.getList()
  }
}
```

**Regra:** um UseCase resolve uma única ação de negócio. Se precisar de "e" na descrição (ex.: "busca lugares e atualiza favoritos"), provavelmente são dois UseCases.

### 4. DataSource (data/datasources)

```typescript
// data/datasources/PlaceRemoteDataSource.ts
import { PlaceDto } from '../models/PlaceDto'
import { httpClient } from '@core/http/httpClient'

export class PlaceRemoteDataSource {
  async fetchList(): Promise<PlaceDto[]> {
    const response = await httpClient.get<PlaceDto[]>('/places')
    return response.data
  }
}
```

### 5. Model/DTO + Mapper (data/models)

```typescript
// data/models/PlaceDto.ts
import { PlaceEntity } from '../../domain/entities/PlaceEntity'

export interface PlaceDto {
  id: string
  name: string
  description: string
  lat: number
  lng: number
}

export const toPlaceEntity = (dto: PlaceDto): PlaceEntity => ({
  id: dto.id,
  name: dto.name,
  description: dto.description,
  coordinates: { latitude: dto.lat, longitude: dto.lng }
})
```

### 6. Repository - Implementação (data/repositories)

```typescript
// data/repositories/PlaceRepositoryImpl.ts
import { PlaceEntity } from '../../domain/entities/PlaceEntity'
import { PlaceRepository } from '../../domain/repositories/PlaceRepository'
import { PlaceRemoteDataSource } from '../datasources/PlaceRemoteDataSource'
import { toPlaceEntity } from '../models/PlaceDto'

export class PlaceRepositoryImpl implements PlaceRepository {
  constructor(private readonly remoteDataSource: PlaceRemoteDataSource) {}

  async getList(): Promise<PlaceEntity[]> {
    const dtos = await this.remoteDataSource.fetchList()
    return dtos.map(toPlaceEntity)
  }

  async getById(id: string): Promise<PlaceEntity | null> {
    const list = await this.getList()
    return list.find((place) => place.id === id) ?? null
  }
}
```

### 7. Composição / DI simples (core/di)

Sem lib pesada de DI (YAGNI). Uma factory function por feature basta:

```typescript
// features/place/di/placeContainer.ts
import { PlaceRemoteDataSource } from '../data/datasources/PlaceRemoteDataSource'
import { PlaceRepositoryImpl } from '../data/repositories/PlaceRepositoryImpl'
import { GetPlaceListUseCase } from '../domain/usecases/GetPlaceListUseCase'

export const makeGetPlaceListUseCase = () => {
  const dataSource = new PlaceRemoteDataSource()
  const repository = new PlaceRepositoryImpl(dataSource)
  return new GetPlaceListUseCase(repository)
}
```

### 8. ViewModel Hook (presentation/viewmodels)

```typescript
// presentation/viewmodels/usePlaceList.ts
import { useCallback, useEffect, useState } from 'react'
import { PlaceEntity } from '../../domain/entities/PlaceEntity'
import { makeGetPlaceListUseCase } from '../../di/placeContainer'

interface UsePlaceListResult {
  places: PlaceEntity[]
  isLoading: boolean
  error: string | null
  refetch: () => Promise<void>
}

const usePlaceList = (): UsePlaceListResult => {
  const [places, setPlaces] = useState<PlaceEntity[]>([])
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false)
  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null)

  const fetchPlaces = useCallback(async () => {
    try {
      setIsLoading(true)
      setError(null)
      const useCase = makeGetPlaceListUseCase()
      const result = await useCase.execute()
      setPlaces(result)
    } catch (err) {
      setError(err instanceof Error ? err.message : 'Unknown error')
    } finally {
      setIsLoading(false)
    }
  }, [])

  useEffect(() => {
    fetchPlaces()
  }, [fetchPlaces])

  return { places, isLoading, error, refetch: fetchPlaces }
}

export default usePlaceList
```

**Nota:** o ViewModel nunca instancia `DataSource`/`RepositoryImpl` diretamente — sempre via factory (`di/`) ou UseCase já pronto, para manter a View/ViewModel isolados de detalhes de `data`.

### 9. View/Screen (presentation/screens)

```typescript
// presentation/screens/PlaceListScreen.tsx
import React from 'react'
import { FlatList, Text, View } from 'react-native'
import usePlaceList from '../viewmodels/usePlaceList'
import { styles } from './styles'

const PlaceListScreen = () => {
  const { places, isLoading, error } = usePlaceList()

  if (error) {
    return <Text style={styles.error}>{error}</Text>
  }

  return (
    <View style={styles.container}>
      <FlatList
        data={places}
        keyExtractor={(place) => place.id}
        refreshing={isLoading}
        renderItem={({ item }) => <Text>{item.name}</Text>}
      />
    </View>
  )
}

export default PlaceListScreen
```

### 10. Templates de Teste por Camada

**Domain (isolado, sem mocks de RN):**

```typescript
// __tests__/domain/GetPlaceListUseCase.test.ts
import { GetPlaceListUseCase } from '../../domain/usecases/GetPlaceListUseCase'
import { PlaceRepository } from '../../domain/repositories/PlaceRepository'

const mockRepository: jest.Mocked<PlaceRepository> = {
  getList: jest.fn(),
  getById: jest.fn()
}

test('should return places from repository', async () => {
  mockRepository.getList.mockResolvedValue([{ id: '1', name: 'Rio', description: '', coordinates: { latitude: 0, longitude: 0 } }])

  const useCase = new GetPlaceListUseCase(mockRepository)
  const result = await useCase.execute()

  expect(result).toHaveLength(1)
})
```

**Data (mockando o datasource):**

```typescript
// __tests__/data/PlaceRepositoryImpl.test.ts
import { PlaceRepositoryImpl } from '../../data/repositories/PlaceRepositoryImpl'
import { PlaceRemoteDataSource } from '../../data/datasources/PlaceRemoteDataSource'

jest.mock('../../data/datasources/PlaceRemoteDataSource')

test('should map dto list to entity list', async () => {
  const dataSource = new PlaceRemoteDataSource() as jest.Mocked<PlaceRemoteDataSource>
  dataSource.fetchList.mockResolvedValue([{ id: '1', name: 'Rio', description: '', lat: 0, lng: 0 }])

  const repository = new PlaceRepositoryImpl(dataSource)
  const result = await repository.getList()

  expect(result[0].coordinates).toEqual({ latitude: 0, longitude: 0 })
})
```

**Presentation (mockando o UseCase/container):**

```typescript
// __tests__/presentation/usePlaceList.test.ts
import { renderHook, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react-native'
import usePlaceList from '../../presentation/viewmodels/usePlaceList'
import * as container from '../../di/placeContainer'

test('should load places on mount', async () => {
  jest.spyOn(container, 'makeGetPlaceListUseCase').mockReturnValue({
    execute: jest.fn().mockResolvedValue([])
  } as any)

  const { result } = renderHook(() => usePlaceList())

  await waitFor(() => expect(result.current.isLoading).toBe(false))
})
```

## 📋 Implementation Checklist

Ao implementar uma nova feature:

- [ ] Criar estrutura de pastas `domain/`, `data/`, `presentation/`
- [ ] Definir Entities em `domain/entities/`
- [ ] Definir Repository (interface) em `domain/repositories/`
- [ ] Implementar UseCases em `domain/usecases/` (um por ação)
- [ ] Implementar DataSource(s) em `data/datasources/`
- [ ] Implementar Repository (implementação) em `data/repositories/`
- [ ] Criar factory/composição em `di/` (ou `core/di/` se compartilhado)
- [ ] Implementar ViewModel (`use[FeatureName].ts`) em `presentation/viewmodels/`
- [ ] Implementar Screen/View em `presentation/screens/`
- [ ] Escrever testes por camada (domain isolado, data com datasource mockado, presentation com usecase mockado)

## 🚫 Anti-patterns

- ❌ `domain` importando de `data`, `presentation`, React ou React Native
- ❌ View/Screen chamando `Repository`/`DataSource` diretamente (deve passar pelo ViewModel → UseCase)
- ❌ UseCase com mais de uma responsabilidade de negócio
- ❌ Lógica de mapeamento DTO→Entity espalhada fora de `data/models`
- ❌ Repository interface e implementação no mesmo arquivo/camada
- ❌ Usar `React.FC`
- ❌ Definir props de View fora de `types.ts`/inline no próprio arquivo do componente sem necessidade

## 📝 Naming Conventions

Ver `.cursor/rules/code-conventions.mdc` seção 1.4 para nomenclatura completa de Entity/UseCase/Repository/DataSource/ViewModel.

